# Badge states nothing can derive (#316): the written-down-debt
# pattern, one line per shield that waits on a human step or is
# exemplary with no data by construction. Everything else in the badge
# block is computed by fix:badges from the tree — see
# scaffold/README-badges.md for the catalogue and the vocabulary.
# bestpractices: 'pending' until the form binds, then the BP_ID.
# reuse: 'pending' until FSFE registration, then 'registered'.
#
# There is deliberately no coverage line. The canon carried
# `coverage exemplary` until #347: it rendered a codecov shield that
# permanently read "unknown", because no bash coverage tool meets the
# belt's priors (tooling-verdicts.md). The shield told a reader
# nothing true — worse, it implied the canon is untested, when
# lint:source-attest drives the real emitter scripts end-to-end
# against recorded fixtures on every commit. What is missing is
# measurement, not tests. The coverage shield now renders iff
# `.coverage-floor` exists, so a repo that cannot measure has no
# shield; the reason lives in tooling-verdicts.md with its reopen
# trigger, which is where it survives the shield's removal.
bestpractices 14058
reuse registered
